%% Reader question: How do completed work and operational learning reinforce one another without silently changing authority?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: reference operating model; public artifacts illustrate selected stages, end-to-end private conformance is not publicly reproducible
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Work and system-learning loops
    accDescr: The work loop turns a durable work item into capability and context routing, side-effect-free planning and validation, a consequence-based authority decision, authorized mutation or action, evidence and verification, and an integrated outcome. Human-gated work waits for a recorded decision and then returns for authority evaluation. Denied work stops and requires a new or materially changed work item. Evidence is a postcondition and never retroactive permission. The system-learning loop turns failures, friction, and observations into versioned constraints, tests and adversarial review, immutable rollout, live enforcement proof, and recurrence measurement. Only reviewed and proven constraints feed future routing.

    subgraph W["Work loop"]
        direction LR
        A["Durable work item"] --> B["Capability and context routing"]
        B --> C["Side-effect-free planning<br/>and validation"]
        C --> D{"Consequence-based<br/>authority decision"}
        D -->|"authorized"| U["Mutation or external action"]
        D -->|"human decision required"| HWAIT["Wait for recorded human decision"]
        HWAIT -->|"recorded decision"| D
        D -->|"denied"| STOP["Stop; new or materially changed<br/>work item required"]
        U --> E["Evidence and verification<br/>postcondition"]
        E --> F["Integrated outcome"]
    end

    subgraph L["System-learning loop"]
        direction LR
        G["Failure, friction, or observation"] --> H["Versioned constraint"]
        H --> I["Tests and adversarial review"]
        I --> J["Immutable rollout"]
        J --> K["Live enforcement proof"]
        K --> M["Recurrence measurement"]
    end

    F --> G
    M -->|"measured learning"| H
    K -->|"proven constraint only"| B
